      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message say what goes wrong without this patch? As far as I can see, smaps reports the wrong `Swap:` for shmem VMAs in 4KB processes in two ways.\n\nFirst, `shmem_swap_usage()` adds `vma_pages()`, which counts 4KB pages since aosp/4312476, to `vm_pgoff`, which counts 16KB pages. So a 16KB `MAP_SHARED` mapping at offset 0 of a 64KB memfd reports the swap of the whole file.\n\nSecond, `smaps_pte_hole()` uses `linear_page_index()`, which rounds both ends of a hole down to a 16KB page. So a hole within one 16KB page counts nothing. If that page is page 0, it counts the swap of the whole file instead, because `end - 1` wraps in `shmem_partial_swap_usage()`.\n\nCould the subject, the body and the comment above the new function also say 4KB VMAs or 4KB processes rather than compat and 4K? Something like `ANDROID: P3S: mm/shmem: Count swapped 4KB VMA bytes by file range`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "ee1c29f8a67aab111e604a51523618a37698f233",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
