      "message": "Nit: could the 4KB case return right after the `!swapped` check, so that the native fast-path condition stays as it is? Something like:\n\n```\n\tif (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma))\n\t\treturn vma_shmem_swap_usage(vma, vma-\u003evm_start, vma-\u003evm_end);\n```\n\nSkipping the `info-\u003eswapped` fast path for 4KB VMAs looks right to me: `vm_slice_off` or a partial last page can leave part of a swapped 16KB page outside the VMA.",
